  is increased which is the biggest issue  with this and many other Windows laptops  if you're going to be using it outside  do you know that you will have to deal  with some glare above the display we  have a 720p webcam that's fairly good  quality but makes video look darker than  in real life on the plus side the audio  quality  is very good for a laptop Mike here's a  sample of the webcam and microphone  quality I was quite surprised most  microphones that are in laptops like  this really cut out the high frequencies  and this one retains that and it sounds  quite a bit better instead of sounding  muffled the speakers are ported to the  sides so they don't get blocked if it's  on your lap they do sound a bit thin but  are surprisingly loud about three  decibels louder than the MacBook Air go  ahead and take a listen for yourself  [Music]  while it doesn't sound great it actually  beats out some Windows laptops that are  two or three times the size the keyboard  features large backlit chiclet keys but  they have low travel and they feel  slightly mushy in my hands-on comparison  I said that I might choose the MacBook  Airs butterfly keyboard over this one  but after spending many hours typing  including this full review I have to say  that I changed my mind  but that's still not saying that much  the trackpad is also decent it is  plastic but it's fairly easy to click  and though it doesn't match up to say a  surface laptop 3 it is about average for  Windows laptops I do wish it was  slightly taller but it makes sense that  it can be because of how small this  machine is I'm glad that Samsung  included a fingerprint scanner built-in  to the power button but I did notice  having to retry my finger more often  than with other laptops but overall it  does work and I'm glad that it's there  now it's time to talk about the biggest  news here and that is the performance of  the mobile Snapdragon ARM processor it's  an 8 core and wrap performance smokes  Apple's latest 