y MacBook could be off for a week  and it loses barely any battery whereas  the Galaxy book s went from 85 percent  down to 25 percent in less than two days  of just being asleep that reminds me  more of smartphones than laptops  I'm not sure if this is a result of the  always-on always ready design the  Microsoft is pushing or something else  the last reason to go arm is the support  for a SIM card so they you can have data  anywhere most laptops don't offer this  and it can be very convenient if you  travel it has a good gigabit modem but I  wasn't able to test it as it only  supports Sprint and Verizon and I have  t-mobile  but speed should be similar to the  higher-end Samsung phones I could  definitely see the galaxy Book s in a  business person's bag or briefcase  taking up almost no room and adding very  little weight and also doing a great job  for email and web use having the freedom  of not having to find Wi-Fi access us  gotta be great and not only because many  hotspots are so slow but also for  security reasons price-wise it's also  very reasonable coming in at lower than  a MacBook Air adult XPS or a surface  laptop three plus the ability to  increase it with microSD you can buy a  good 512 gigabyte microSD card with  fairly reasonable speeds for only $95.00  I'll go ahead and drop a link for you  guys down below this is something that  you can't do with the MacBook Air or  with most Windows laptops even if they  offer a card they were gonna stick way  out which isn't practical for daily  attached storage so now taking an honest  why the overall look at the  machine in most areas like the display  the keyboard the speaker's trackpad  webcam and the general performance of  this galaxy book s it is just good  enough but not really good in anything  but the battery life because of that I  think that if you don't need to stand  out features like battery life and LTE I  would absolutely recommend one of two  Ultrabook laptops that I link down in  the video 